"# Field Notes — Project contract

## Product brief

Build the project described below from a fresh repository. Treat this contract as the project brief. Keep the implementation self-contained; do not depend on another project’s source code or private configuration.

### Purpose

> A small notebook for independent researchers to collect observations\\.

### Intended users

> Independent researchers

### MVP requirements

> Create and organize notes\\.
> Search existing observations\\.

### Out of scope

> Team collaboration and billing

## Stack and structure

Use TypeScript, React, TanStack Start with Vite, and pnpm. Build the interface with Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui. Use mutually compatible stable versions and commit the lockfile. Keep modules cohesive and expose documented development and production build commands. Start with one application package; organize source by feature.

## Infrastructure

### Deployment target

Deliver a locally runnable Node.js application. Document pnpm install, pnpm dev, the production build, and the supported Node.js start command using TanStack Start’s Nitro deployment adapter. Document setup for selected services. No production hosting target is selected.

## UI / UX

### Interface direction

Use a minimal visual style with sidebar navigation. Set the theme to follow the system preference and use a neutral primary palette.

Keep the design barebones, clear, and functional. Prioritize the core task over decorative elements.

Use responsive layouts, visible keyboard focus, labeled controls, accessible contrast, and clear loading, empty, error, and success states.

### Core screens

> Notes list, note editor, settings
"
`;

